---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { QRGeneratorShell } from "../../components/qr/QRGeneratorShell";
import Card from "../../components/ui/Card";
---

<Layout title="Free WiFi QR Code Generator - Real QR Code Generator" description="Share local wireless networks with guests securely. Scan to connect to home or office Wi-Fi without typing passwords. Free vector downloads.">
  <div class="py-12 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-link-bg-soft text-link text-xs font-mono font-medium mb-4">
      WIFI GENERATOR
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mb-6">
      Free WiFi QR Code Generator.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-body">
      Share your local network credentials securely. Generate custom style codes that connect phones to your home or office Wi-Fi automatically upon scanning.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Interactive Customizer preloaded with WiFi -->
  <div class="py-6 mb-20">
    <QRGeneratorShell client:load defaultType="wifi" />
  </div>

  <!-- SEO structured copy block -->
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 space-y-12 pb-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4">How does a WiFi QR code work?</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          WiFi QR codes encode your network name (SSID), security type (such as WPA or WEP), and password in a standardized text structure: <code>WIFI:S:NetworkName;T:WPA;P:SecretPassword;;</code>. When an iPhone or Android camera scans this matrix, it interprets the security configuration and prompts the user to join the network.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4">Is it safe to share my Wi-Fi via QR?</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          Yes! The QR code does not broadcast your credentials over the internet; it simply stores the text locally in the visual pattern. Only users who physically scan the printed card or screen can read the barcode data to connect.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Card level={2} rounded="lg" className="bg-canvas p-8">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">SSID & Password Tips</h3>
      <ul class="text-sm text-body space-y-3 list-disc list-inside leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong>Exact spelling matches:</strong> Ensure your network SSID name exactly matches case-sensitivity (e.g. <code>MyWiFi</code> vs <code>mywifi</code>) or the scan connection will fail.</li>
        <li><strong>Hidden Networks:</strong> If your router broadcasts a hidden SSID, some mobile devices may require you to select "Hidden Network" manual options, although standard setups join automatically.</li>
        <li><strong>Print & Frame:</strong> Download as a clean SVG, print, and place inside your guest rooms or office lounge for a premium user experience.</li>
      </ul>
    </Card>
  </div>
</Layout>
